            "review_title": "Review at BOHO Seafood Restaurant Vũng Tàu",
            "review_text": "Excursion12283188446\n1 contribution\n0\nGreat for family\nMar 2026 • Family\nI’m usually quite picky when it comes to seafood restaurants, especially in tourist areas, but BOHO honestly exceeded my expectations.\n\nThe first thing I noticed was the location — right by the sea with an open view and good airflow. It doesn’t feel overcrowded or overly commercial like many places nearby.\n\nThe seafood was fresh, which is non-negotiable for me. You can actually see the live tanks, and the quality shows in the taste. That said, some dishes could be a bit more refined in seasoning — not bad at all, just slightly on the simpler side.\n\nService was generally good. Staff were polite and tried their best, although during peak hours things slowed down a little. Nothing too frustrating, just something to be aware of if you come at a busy time.\n\nPrices are reasonable considering the location and quality. Not cheap, but fair.\n\nOverall, a solid experience. With a bit more consistency in execution, this place could easily be one of the top seafood spots in Vung Tau.\n\nWould still recommend\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 17, 2026",
